CORAL inference, 2026.

The inference runtime is adapted from Protenix (ByteDance and contributors):
https://github.com/bytedance/Protenix
The upstream Apache-2.0 license and source attribution are retained in vendor/.
Protenix includes Apache-2.0 code adapted from OpenFold, OneFlow and FastFold,
as described in vendor/LICENSE and the original source headers.

CORAL adaptations include fibril PF/layer relative-position encoding,
fixed-receptor/constraint inference, portable input and asset handling,
input-chemistry ligand export, and confidence-rank-consistent structure export.
The vendored Python files carry a distribution modification notice.

The supplied model is the CORAL mix3 step-19999 checkpoint from the
Protenix v0.5 model family. It is not the Protenix-v2 model.
Code and CORAL checkpoint are distributed under Apache-2.0.
Chemical Component Dictionary data is from wwPDB, with an RDKit cache derived
from it. See https://www.wwpdb.org/data/ccd and
https://www.wwpdb.org/about/usage-policies for source attribution and terms.
Example receptor/reference structures are derived from PDB entries 7WMM,
8UQ7, 9O4B and 7YNF (fibrils), and 5SD5/HWI and 5SIS/JSM (PoseBusters).
Per-example reference/source.json records symmetry-generated neighboring
ligand copies where applicable. References are used for visualization;
blind inference does not consume the reference receptor or ligand coordinates.
